KNOWNBUG (template-argument / qualified-id pack-expansion path): a deduced
function-template parameter pack A used as a class-template argument
(first_type<A...>) is not expanded into the class template's own parameter pack
during nested instantiation, so the dependent qualified-id first_type<A...>::type
does not resolve and the instantiated body is dropped (nondet return).

Decltype-free, header-free isolation of the path also exercised (with a
decltype-valued member) by cpp11_decltype_pack_in_class_template.  Part of the
unified pack-expansion rework documented in
doc/architectural/cpp-variadic-pack-expansion-rework.md.  Reclassify CORE once
the deduced pack is expanded as a class-template argument.
